 ## Overview
-Deformable and Dynamic Fields extend static radiance field optimization to model scenes that change over time or undergo non-rigid deformation [912-neural-volumes.md][5540-endonerf.md]. Unlike static methods that assume a fixed geometry, these methods introduce a temporal or deformation component to map input coordinates to a canonical space, enabling the synthesis of novel views for moving or deforming objects [912-neural-volumes.md][5540-endonerf.md]. They are distinguished from static voxel methods (e.g., DeepVoxels) and static MLP-based methods (e.g., NeRF) by their explicit handling of motion, either through learned warp fields or displacement mappings [912-neural-volumes.md][5540-endonerf.md].
